#
# Remove an obstacle previously spawned by SpawnObstacle.
#
# Served as /faults/clear_obstacle by ral_faults/fault_manager.py (Phase 4.1).
# Injection point: /world/<world>/remove (gz UserCommands).
#
# `name` must be the name the obstacle was spawned under, and must match
# SpawnObstacle's [A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}. Removing a name that was
# never spawned is a failure, not a no-op: a silent success would let a run
# report a cleared fault that never existed.
#
# `fault_id` is the join key for this fault instance: the value the caller will
# see again on every FaultEvent the manager publishes for it. The scenario
# runner sends the id it minted (<kind>_<1-based index after sorting by
# at_sec>, scenario.py:308). An EMPTY string means "allocate one", which is
# what the dashboard sends; the manager answers with <kind>_ui_<n>. The
# RESPONSE carries the id the manager used - the one sent, or the minted one
# when the request left it empty. The manager also publishes `cleared` for the
# SPAWN's id, so both ids appear.

string fault_id
string name
---
string fault_id
bool success
string message
